WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-26, with W28 (help builtin)


STATE

  Version 0.3.9 adds the `help` builtin, printing a usage guide for
  tam-clam and a complete table of keybindings. Version 0.3.8 loads ~/.rc
  before the first interactive prompt (--norc skips it). The guidance
  builtin prints the same key help as the Ctrl+G overlay. Normal and
  sanitizer suites pass.

  Phase P4 complete (arrays, [[ ]]/=~, local/declare,
  brace expansion, process substitution, ** globstar, strict modes,
  abbreviations, man-page completion generator, and -v / --version), on
  branch dev.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test, make sanitize, and make
  fuzz pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; the Tamlinux-wide keybinding standard lives in
  tam-idol/keys/keybindings.md and tam-clam implements it in
  keys/keybindings.md (no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\,
  VSUSP=Ctrl+P, Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the
  function recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a
  reported error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret
  backslash escapes by default; ** recursive globbing is off by default;
  strict modes are opt-in and off by default.


